
update products set
  quick_answer = 'Semaglutide (CAS 910463-68-2) is a GLP-1 receptor agonist studied extensively in metabolic research relating to appetite regulation and glucose homeostasis, supplied here as an 8mg pen kit strictly for laboratory and in-vitro research use. It is not the licensed pharmaceutical product sold as Ozempic, Wegovy, or Rybelsus — this listing is an unlicensed research-use product supplied outside the pharmacy/prescription system, and the MHRA has separately warned about falsified and mislabelled semaglutide-type pens circulating online.',
  content_sections = '[{"heading": null, "body": "Semaglutide is unusual among the compounds on this site because it is also sold, under separate brand names, as a licensed prescription medicine. That makes it easy for listings to blur the line between a genuine research-use product and an implied substitute for a doctor-prescribed treatment. <strong>Synedica Semaglutide GLP-1 Pen Kit</strong> is sold on the same research-use basis as every other peptide on this site — not as, and not a substitute for, any licensed medicine. This page sets out the chemistry, what published clinical research on semaglutide has found, and what UK regulators have said about counterfeit and mislabelled semaglutide-type products sold outside pharmacy channels."}, {"heading": "What Semaglutide Is", "body": "Semaglutide is a 31-amino-acid analogue of human glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1), modified with an amino-isobutyric acid substitution for resistance to DPP-4 breakdown and a C18 fatty-diacid side chain that binds reversibly to albumin, extending its half-life to roughly a week. This makes it structurally and pharmacokinetically distinct from short unmodified research peptides such as BPC-157 or GHK-Cu. It carries CAS number 910463-68-2, molecular formula C187H291N45O59, and a molecular weight of approximately 4,113.6 g/mol.<br /><br />As a GLP-1 receptor agonist, semaglutide is studied for its effects on appetite regulation, gastric emptying, and glucose-dependent insulin secretion — mechanisms relevant to metabolic research rather than a claim about what this listing does for any individual."}, {"heading": "What Current Research Says", "body": "The best-known clinical data on semaglutide comes from the STEP and SUSTAIN trial programmes. STEP 1 (Wilding et al., 2021, <em>New England Journal of Medicine</em>) randomised 1,961 adults with overweight or obesity to once-weekly semaglutide 2.4mg or placebo for 68 weeks; the semaglutide group had a mean body-weight change of −14.9% versus −2.4% with placebo, an estimated treatment difference of −12.4 percentage points. The SUSTAIN trial programme separately evaluated semaglutide for type 2 diabetes at lower doses.<br /><br />These are clinical trial results for the licensed pharmaceutical product administered under medical supervision at a defined, regulated dose — they describe what has been studied about the active substance, not a claim about this unlicensed research-use listing, which is not administered, supervised, or dosed in the way the trial protocol specifies."}, {"heading": "Regulatory Status in the UK", "body": "Semaglutide holds MHRA marketing authorisations as <strong>Ozempic</strong> (type 2 diabetes) and <strong>Wegovy</strong> (weight management), both Prescription Only Medicines, with <strong>Rybelsus</strong> as an oral form. This listing is not any of those products. It is an unlicensed research-use vial of the same active substance, sold outside the pharmacy and prescriber system — with no MHRA batch release, no prescriber oversight, and no verified sterility or dosing accuracy.<br /><br />The MHRA''s <a href=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/655f50981fd90c0013ac3ac5/November_2023-DSU.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">November 2023 Drug Safety Update</a> reported 369 falsified Ozempic pens seized in the UK by October 2023 (up from zero before January 2023), 16 Yellow Card adverse-event reports by 20 November 2023, and five confirmed cases where pens were relabelled with insulin instead of semaglutide or liraglutide, resulting in hospitalisation for hypoglycaemic shock. That warning concerned falsified branded pens specifically, not research-use listings — but it illustrates the same underlying risk that applies to any semaglutide-type product obtained outside the regulated supply chain: there is no independent guarantee that the vial contains what the label says. This listing is supplied strictly for laboratory and in-vitro research use, is not licensed under the <a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2012/1916\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Human Medicines Regulations 2012 (SI 2012/1916)</a>, and has not been assessed by the MHRA for safety or efficacy under this listing."}, {"heading": "Specifications", "body": "<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;\"><thead><tr><th style=\"text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding:6px 8px;\">Property</th><th style=\"text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding:6px 8px;\">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">CAS number</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">910463-68-2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Molecular formula</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">C187H291N45O59</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Molecular weight</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">≈ 4,113.6 g/mol</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Structure</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">31-amino-acid GLP-1 analogue with C18 fatty-diacid albumin-binding side chain</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Receptor activity</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">GLP-1 receptor agonist</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Form supplied</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;\">Pen kit, 8mg</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;\">UK legal / regulatory status</td><td style=\"padding:6px 8px;\">Same active substance is licensed as Ozempic/Wegovy (POM) — this listing is an unlicensed research-use product, not those products, not MHRA-approved, supplied strictly for laboratory research</td></tr></tbody></table><br />The CAS number and molecular formula are independently verifiable against public chemical databases such as PubChem."}, {"heading": "Purity, Batch Testing and Certificate of Analysis Standards", "body": "Every <strong>Synedica Semaglutide GLP-1 Pen Kit</strong> unit offered for sale is supplied with third-party analytical documentation confirming peptide identity and purity, the analytical method used (typically HPLC or mass spectrometry), the batch or lot number, and the issuing laboratory. Given the MHRA''s documented findings of pens mislabelled with the wrong active substance entirely, verifying that a listing''s CAS number, molecular formula, and COA are independently checkable matters more for semaglutide than for peptides with no licensed counterpart. See our <a href=\"/contact\">contact page</a> to request a Certificate of Analysis for a specific batch."}, {"heading": "Sourcing and Verification", "body": "Before ordering, check that a listing states research-use status clearly rather than implying it is a substitute for Ozempic, Wegovy, or a prescriber-supervised weight-management programme, that batch documentation is offered rather than promised only “on request,” and that the compound''s identity (CAS number, molecular formula) is independently verifiable against a source such as PubChem. <strong>Synedica Semaglutide GLP-1 Pen Kit</strong> is offered for sale on this basis, with documentation available per batch. Researchers examining other GLP-1 and metabolic-research peptides may also find <a href=\"/product/synedica-retatrutide-40mg-injection-kit\">Synedica Retatrutide 40mg</a> and <a href=\"/product/synedica-tirzepatide-40mg-injection-pen-kit\">Synedica Tirzepatide 40mg</a> relevant, and the full catalogue is browsable on the <a href=\"/products\">research products page</a>."}]'::jsonb,
  faq = '[{"question": "Is this the same as Ozempic or Wegovy?", "answer": "No. Ozempic and Wegovy are MHRA-licensed, Prescription Only Medicines containing semaglutide, dispensed through pharmacies under prescriber supervision. This listing is an unlicensed research-use product supplied outside that system, with no MHRA batch release or prescriber oversight, and it is not sold or marketed as a substitute for either product."}, {"question": "Is it legal to buy semaglutide without a prescription in the UK?", "answer": "Semaglutide as Ozempic, Wegovy, or Rybelsus is a Prescription Only Medicine and can only lawfully be obtained via a prescriber. This listing is sold as an unlicensed research chemical strictly for laboratory and in-vitro research use, not for human application, and has not been assessed by the MHRA for safety or efficacy under this listing."}, {"question": "Why is this semaglutide product sold as “research use only”?", "answer": "Because it is an unlicensed product: it has not gone through the MHRA marketing-authorisation process that Ozempic and Wegovy have, is not manufactured or batch-released as a medicine, and is not dispensed under prescriber supervision. It is supplied strictly for laboratory and in-vitro research."}, {"question": "Has the MHRA warned about counterfeit or mislabelled semaglutide products?", "answer": "Yes. The MHRA''s November 2023 Drug Safety Update reported 369 falsified Ozempic pens seized in the UK by October 2023, and five confirmed cases where pens were relabelled with insulin instead of semaglutide or liraglutide, leading to hospitalisation for hypoglycaemic shock. That warning concerned falsified branded pens, not research-use listings specifically, but it illustrates the same risk of obtaining any semaglutide-type product outside the regulated supply chain."}, {"question": "How do I know a semaglutide vial actually contains what the label says?", "answer": "Request a Certificate of Analysis confirming identity and purity by an independent testing method (typically HPLC or mass spectrometry), and independently verify the CAS number (910463-68-2) and molecular formula (C187H291N45O59) against a source such as PubChem. The MHRA''s findings of pens mislabelled with the wrong active substance make this verification step particularly important for semaglutide-type products."}, {"question": "What has clinical research found about semaglutide?", "answer": "The STEP 1 trial (Wilding et al., 2021, New England Journal of Medicine) randomised 1,961 adults to once-weekly semaglutide 2.4mg or placebo for 68 weeks and reported a mean body-weight change of −14.9% versus −2.4% with placebo. This describes the licensed pharmaceutical product administered under medical supervision at a defined dose, not this unlicensed research-use listing."}, {"question": "What does the Certificate of Analysis (COA) show for this product?", "answer": "A COA confirms peptide identity and purity, the analytical testing method used (typically HPLC or mass spectrometry), the batch or lot number, and the issuing laboratory."}, {"question": "How is the CAS number used to verify this compound?", "answer": "CAS 910463-68-2 identifies semaglutide. Researchers can cross-check this number, along with the molecular formula C187H291N45O59, against an independent database such as PubChem to confirm chemical identity before use."}, {"question": "Does the pen kit format affect the research application?", "answer": "The pen kit is a delivery/packaging format only. This listing makes no dosing, administration, or reconstitution recommendations; researchers determine their own protocols in line with their institution''s research and safety governance."}, {"question": "How should this product be stored before use?", "answer": "Store according to the conditions printed on the batch documentation and product label. Exact storage parameters and shelf life are batch-specific and confirmed on the accompanying documentation."}, {"question": "Can this product be used as a weight-loss treatment or diabetes medicine?", "answer": "No. It is sold strictly for laboratory and in-vitro research use. It is not a substitute for Ozempic, Wegovy, or any prescribed treatment, is not for human or veterinary use or application, is not licensed under the Human Medicines Regulations 2012, and has not been assessed by the MHRA for safety or efficacy under this listing."}, {"question": "Where can I buy semaglutide for research use?", "answer": "It is available for sale directly from Synedica UK, supplied with batch documentation and third-party testing for verified UK research buyers."}]'::jsonb,
